  "scope": "# Review: ead22faa41ef public-batch reconciliation\nTask/source: `ead22faa41ef`; production generator `3.1.0`, SHA-256 `ffcf07292e27f9a5788fe93109327ec123b281d8c35797dfa6f007c33c09dfd9`.\nDefect: the proposed survivor-role exporter hashed and masked public payloads correctly, but physically created them in private role/seed order.\nRepair: plan both episodes in memory, reject duplicate visible IDs before creating the destination, then publish public files in lexicographic public-ID order.\nPreserved: private episode numbering/report order, all labels, Racket programs, production generator, and canonical rule `6615d26334ba` are unchanged.\nFocused regression: reversed private role order now yields sorted public writes; duplicate visible content raises before any destination exists.\nScoped tests: 26 passed plus 14 subtests; the only warning is an inherited `GenCtx._drawn` deprecation in an unchanged production test.\nRacket replay: 4 canonical labels and 14 episode labels passed; 2 public files and both parameter settings verified.\nTickets: the four-query privacy boundary was confirmed without approval promotion; a lawful Racket witness refuted plain vertical duplication for `7f181d3b0012`.\nRemaining limits: the survivor-role family is still proposed/unapproved, and this writer-only repair does not clear inherited teaching audits.\nDisposition: scoped reconciliation complete; routine maintainer review, with no production or training-admission claim.\n",
